From 7c2decc7358ff6ecce8d9ebb441487de05d09ade Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 19:59:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07302/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5729: GTV
 validation-gate tolerance matched-budget A/B

Tests whether loosening GroundTruthValidatedFrameChangeScorer's
zero-tolerance-forever validation criterion recovers live-agent capability,
extending exp5590 (dict-candidate fix null) and exp5728 (cnn_weight sweep null,
which localized this gate as the next lever). Rate-tolerance gate (0.6/0.7/0.8)
+ reset-on-level-up vs baseline, 11-game roster, budget 200, no-LLM harness.

Result: the rate gate turns the scorer ON (3/11 -> 9-10/11 games validated,
ranking consults ~3x) with NO safety regression (states dropped 6-8%) and
protection preserved (sk48 at 0.056 agreement stays gated off), but banks no
extra levels -- on lp85 the validated scorer is consulted ~27k times yet search
is byte-identical, because the memory-dominated blend is near-uniform. Confirms
exp5728's retire condition: the blocker is now DOWNSTREAM (scorer signal
quality), not the gate. reset_on_levelup is byte-identical to baseline (no game
reaches L2). Live-default change is operator-only; recommendation is NOT to
change on a capability basis. adversarial_verify: 0 flags.

